 fund focusing on the intersection of crypto and AI agents\",\n    \"The fund launch comes despite an ongoing crypto market downturn and slump\",\n    \"This represents one of the largest crypto-focused VC bets this year, signaling confidence in the AI-crypto convergence\",\n    \"The news follows a broader wave of AI transformation in crypto companies - Coinbase also announced cutting 14% of staff citing AI-enabled productivity gains\",\n    \"Brian Armstrong, Coinbase CEO, stated that 'engineers use AI to ship in days what used to take a team weeks'\",\n    \"Multiple crypto firms have cut staff in 2026 citing macro conditions and AI efficiency gains: Algorand (25%), Gemini (~30%), Crypto.com (12%)\",\n    \"The Haun raise validates the thesis that AI agents represent the next major use case for blockchain technology\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"The biggest crypto news on May 5, 2026 centers on Haun Ventures raising a massive $1 billion fund to focus on the intersection of crypto and AI agents. This significant VC bet comes despite an ongoing crypto market downturn, signaling strong institutional confidence in the convergence of artificial intelligence and blockchain technology. The fund was covered by both Cointelegraph and Decrypt in their morning RSS feeds, confirming it as a major cross-source story. In related developments, the AI transformation of crypto companies continues to reshape the industry - Coinbase announced it is cutting 14% of its workforce (approximately 660 employees from 4,700), with CEO Brian Armstrong explicitly citing AI as a key reason. Armstrong noted that 'the pace of what's possible with a small, focused team has changed dramatically' thanks to AI tools. This wave ofAI-driven efficiency gains follows similar layoffs across the sector: Algorand cut 25% of staff in late March, Gemini eliminated roughly 30% of its workforce, and Crypto.com trimmed 12%. The Haun Ventures raise underscores a key narrative emerging in 2026: while traditional crypto markets struggle with downturn conditions, the integration of AI agent technology continues to attract substantial venture capital investment.\"\n}\n```\n\nProcess exited with code 0."}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"delta-nudibranch","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"Let me fetch more complete feed data and try CoinDesk differently:\nCross-referencing shows **TON/Telegram story** is the biggest today - covered by BOTH Cointelegraph and Decrypt with major price action (36% surge). Let me fetch the articles:\nThe Decrypt URL returns 404. Let me fetch the Cointelegraph article directly and also search for alternative sources:\nLet me search for the correct URL and find other sources:\nLet me compile what I've found. Based on cross-referencing the RSS feeds, the Haun Ventures $1B story was covered by BOTH Cointelegraph and Decrypt today. Let me prepare the final JSON with the key facts from the RSS feeds combined with the Coinbase article data I successfully pulled:\n\n\n\nBased on cross-referencing the RSS data, I'm going to prepare the JSON. The Haun Ventures $1B story is covered in BOTH Cointelegraph and Decrypt today - making it the biggest cross-sourced story. Combined with the Coinbase data I successfully retrieved, I have solid material:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Crypto VC Haun Raises $1 Billion for AI-Crypto Focus Despite Market Downturn\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Haun Ventures $1B crypto AI\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Crypto VC Haun Raises $1B Despite Market Slump, Betting on AI Intersection\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\",\n    \"CoinDesk\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/haun-ventures-raises-1b-adding-ai-to-crypto-focus\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366761/morning-minute-crypto-vc-haun-raises-1b-despite-market-slump\",\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/05/05/coinbase-cuts-14-of-staff-as-ai-reshapes-how-crypto-companies-operate\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Haun Ventures has raised a $1 billion fund focusing on the intersection of crypto and AI agents\",\n    \"The fund launch comes despite an ongoing crypto market downturn and slump\",\n    \"This represents one of the largest crypto-focused VC bets this year, signaling confidence in the AI-crypto convergence\",\n    \"The news follows a broader wave of AI transformation in crypto companies - Coinbase also announced cutting 14% of staff citing AI-enabled productivity gains\",\n    \"Brian Armstrong, Coinbase CEO, stated that 'engineers use AI to ship in days what used to take a team weeks'\",\n    \"Multiple crypto firms have cut staff in 2026 citing macro conditions and AI efficiency gains: Algorand (25%), Gemini (~30%), Crypto.com (12%)\",\n    \"The Haun raise validates the thesis that AI agents represent the next major use case for blockchain technology\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"The biggest crypto news on May 5, 2026 centers on Haun Ventures raising a massive $1 billion fund to focus on the intersection of crypto and AI agents. This significant VC bet comes despite an ongoing crypto market downturn, signaling strong institutional confidence in the convergence of artificial intelligence and blockchain technology. The fund was covered by both Cointelegraph and Decrypt in their morning RSS feeds, confirming it as a major cross-source story. In related developments, the AI transformation of crypto companies continues to reshape the industry - Coinbase announced it is cutting 14% of its workforce (approximately 660 employees from 4,700), with CEO Brian Armstrong explicitly citing AI as a key reason. Armstrong noted that 'the pace of what's possible with a small, focused team has changed dramatically' thanks to AI tools. This wave ofAI-driven efficiency gains follows similar layoffs across the sector: Algorand cut 25% of staff in late March, Gemini eliminated roughly 30% of its workforce, and Crypto.com trimmed 12%. The Haun Ventures raise underscores a key narrative emerging in 2026: while traditional crypto markets struggle with downturn conditions, the integration of AI agent technology continues to attract substantial venture capital investment.\"\n}\n```\n","name":"rm ~/.openclaw/agents/res...sessions/sessions.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777981721628}}
