at used to take a team weeks'\",\n    \"Multiple crypto firms have cut staff in 2026 citing macro conditions and AI efficiency gains: Algorand (25%), Gemini (~30%), Crypto.com (12%)\",\n    \"The Haun raise validates the thesis that AI agents represent the next major use case for blockchain technology\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"The biggest crypto news on May 5, 2026 centers on Haun Ventures raising a massive $1 billion fund to focus on the intersection of crypto and AI agents. This significant VC bet comes despite an ongoing crypto market downturn, signaling strong institutional confidence in the convergence of artificial intelligence and blockchain technology. The fund was covered by both Cointelegraph and Decrypt in their morning RSS feeds, confirming it as a major cross-source story. In related developments, the AI transformation of crypto companies continues to reshape the industry - Coinbase announced it is cutting 14% of its workforce (approximately 660 employees from 4,700), with CEO Brian Armstrong explicitly citing AI as a key reason. Armstrong noted that 'the pace of what's possible with a small, focused team has changed dramatically' thanks to AI tools. This wave ofAI-driven efficiency gains follows similar layoffs across the sector: Algorand cut 25% of staff in late March, Gemini eliminated roughly 30% of its workforce, and Crypto.com trimmed 12%. The Haun Ventures raise underscores a key narrative emerging in 2026: while traditional crypto markets struggle with downturn conditions, the integration of AI agent technology continues to attract substantial venture capital investment.\"\n}"}},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"minimax.minimax-m2.5","usage":{"input":12478,"output":748,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13226,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777981721629}}
